KG42.register("source_edge_archive-872cc9a713cfe5fd9b173c5d",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E002","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-a9bd9e360b96ff06","target":"KG31-623d45f464e9bce4","source_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","target_occurrence_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","source_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::bidding.supply","target_unit_id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. | Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. | Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework. | SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g06-e12","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"121ae981fec75a4615e7a7240bb213f22d0c0e4787ac36b6204317b17ae97a58","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The coordinator limits supply-bid updates by evenly randomly selecting a predefined-size set of participants forbidden to change their energy bids at each iteration. Scope: Optional bid-count step length control in iterative P2P energy bidding; selection covers all participants and applies to supply bids among their submissions. Condition: Bid-count control is adopted; the supply bid belongs to a participant selected into the forbidden set. The coordinator must reject a supply bid whose change exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. Scope: Proposed practical coordinator enforcement of optional bid-ramping control in P2P energy bidding. Condition: The proposed enforcement rule is adopted and a supply bid exceeds the prescribed ramping-rate limit. SDR supply bids follow the energy-bid content specification in Formula (A18), derived from the participant's decision-making-model results. Scope: Supply quantities represented within SDR energy bids during the iterative bidding process. Condition: The energy bid is negative at the relevant time step. Supply-bid changes at each iteration must respect the prescribed ramping allowance around the previous bid, with the resulting bounds clipped to the minimum and maximum energy-bid limits. Scope: Supply energy-bid constraints in the simulation's iterative decision-making model. Condition: The bid-ramping form of optional step length control is adopted. The two controls may be combined by first limiting the number of bids allowed to change and then limiting changes to the allowable supply bids. Scope: Supply-bid updates under optional combined step length control. Condition: Bid-count control and bid-ramping control are used together.","target_definition":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices. Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step.","expression":"e^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^{*} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must\\text{-}run} - P_{PV,t},\\; t \\in T \\right\\} \\quad (A18); \\quad \\mathcal{PA}^{-}_{t} = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0,\\; n \\in \\mathcal{PA} \\} \\quad (A22)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"p g y ⎫ ∈ T ⎬⎭ (A18) he decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)–(A17). With the energy ell","equation_id":"A18","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the SDR mechanism, prosumers are required to provide energy bids for the coordinator at every iteration. Specifically, based on the results of the decision-making model presented in Section A.1, the energy bid of a prosumer is given by\n\ne^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must-run} - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\right\\}  (A18)\n\nin which x^* = \\{x_{\\delta,t}^*, x_t^{ch*}, x_t^{dis*}\\}, \\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f, t \\in T are the optimal solution of the decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)-(A17)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"(A22) (A23) il price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR haring r","equation_id":"A19-A23","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids from all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal selling price by\n\np_t^{sell} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{r_t^{export} \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{(r_t^{retail} - r_t^{export}) \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{export}}, & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A19)\n\nand the internal buying price by\n\np_t^{buy} = \\begin{cases} p_t^{sell} \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{retail}(1 - SDR_t), & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A20)\n\nin which\n\nSDR_t = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}  (A21)\n\nwhere\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}  (A22)\n\nand\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+ = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}.  (A23)\n\nIn Formulas (A19)-(A23), r_t^{export} and r_t^{retail} are the export and retail price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR represents the supply and demand ratio of the whole P2P energy sharing region. Formulas (A19)-(A23) establish the pricing model in the coordinator agent under the SDR mechanism."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. | Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. | Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework. | SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g06-e12","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"paper_scope_note":"SDR, MMR, and BS are kept separate; the A18 net quantity differs from the A24 independent component; optional step-size control and the divergent loop in the example are not treated as general convergence or necessary dependencies."}});
